1
00:00:14,440 --> 00:00:25,480
Catching the wind of the seasons as they come round,
a dazzling, greatest debut

2
00:00:26,940 --> 00:00:37,460
Easily leaping over the hectic times,
diving into town with hero airs

3
00:00:37,460 --> 00:00:39,660
I wanna time with you for a night

4
00:00:39,660 --> 00:00:45,080
Like we're only putting on the quick,
fashionable things

5
00:00:45,080 --> 00:00:49,180
Because your bare face suits you best

6
00:00:49,720 --> 00:00:50,780
Let it ring

7
00:00:51,700 --> 00:00:55,020
Everybody can do, I started running

8
00:00:55,020 --> 00:00:58,240
Dreams never stop, you know

9
00:00:58,240 --> 00:01:02,480
Let's set out on the voyage tomorrow too

10
00:01:02,480 --> 00:01:03,380
Let it run

11
00:01:03,380 --> 00:01:07,660
Everybody can do a little bit

12
00:01:07,660 --> 00:01:10,820
It doesn't hurt even if you stick out

13
00:01:10,820 --> 00:01:15,020
Holding onto a noisy curiosity

14
00:01:15,680 --> 00:01:18,060
I was able to fly strong and high

15
00:01:28,260 --> 00:01:30,840
Great Cockroach Race

16
00:01:36,500 --> 00:01:38,300
Look, look at this!

17
00:01:38,300 --> 00:01:40,740
These are the results from the
other day's health checkup, right?

18
00:01:41,200 --> 00:01:42,680
What about them?

19
00:01:42,680 --> 00:01:44,580
Your blood sugar is high.

20
00:01:44,580 --> 00:01:47,000
You should watch out for diabetes.

21
00:01:47,000 --> 00:01:48,280
Where are you looking?

22
00:01:48,280 --> 00:01:49,200
Here, right here!

23
00:01:49,200 --> 00:01:52,060
Your physical fitness is
on par with a 35-year-old.

24
00:01:52,860 --> 00:01:55,360
Thirty-five, I tell you, thirty-five!

25
00:01:56,120 --> 00:01:57,380
You're young for your age.

26
00:01:57,380 --> 00:01:59,400
Do you have some kind of secret?

27
00:02:01,160 --> 00:02:07,100
Actually, about three months ago I started
going to an athletic club to build my strength.

28
00:02:07,100 --> 00:02:08,780
An athletic club

29
00:02:09,500 --> 00:02:13,480
That's right. A friend invited me,
and it's really working.

30
00:02:13,480 --> 00:02:15,680
I won't lose to you young whippersnappers.

31
00:02:15,680 --> 00:02:18,280
I won't lose even to Ryotsu!

32
00:02:18,280 --> 00:02:21,160
Speaking of which, the Chief seems
to be looking healthier lately.

33
00:02:21,700 --> 00:02:23,800
Right? My stiff shoulders
have gotten better, too.

34
00:02:24,280 --> 00:02:26,460
How about you try it too, Terai?

35
00:02:26,980 --> 00:02:29,684
But someone like me who barely exercises...

36
00:02:29,734 --> 00:02:31,800
might just end up more exhausted, right?

37
00:02:31,800 --> 00:02:33,280
Don't worry about that.

38
00:02:33,280 --> 00:02:35,898
First, they check your
fitness with a computer,

39
00:02:35,948 --> 00:02:39,460
and then you start with a
menu suited to your level.

40
00:02:40,220 --> 00:02:41,960
Well, you've really done a fine job of it.

41
00:02:45,720 --> 00:02:47,640
Morning, Mom... I mean, Chief.

42
00:02:48,560 --> 00:02:50,380
What do you mean, "good morning"?

43
00:02:50,380 --> 00:02:53,360
I see your irregular
lifestyle still hasn't changed.

44
00:02:53,860 --> 00:02:56,600
Do you really think you can carry
out your duties properly like that?

45
00:02:57,300 --> 00:02:59,100
There's no need to worry, sir.

46
00:02:59,100 --> 00:03:00,680
I'm confident in my stamina.

47
00:03:01,080 --> 00:03:03,680
Why, just now I stayed up two
nights straight building a model kit,

48
00:03:04,180 --> 00:03:07,340
the night before that I
beat two new video games,

49
00:03:07,340 --> 00:03:09,720
and before that I drank
all night with my friends.

50
00:03:10,120 --> 00:03:10,960
Bakabon!

51
00:03:15,040 --> 00:03:17,460
Your voice does seem
more powerful than usual.

52
00:03:17,460 --> 00:03:19,620
I guess this is the result
of the athletic training too.

53
00:03:20,000 --> 00:03:20,940
Athletic?

54
00:03:21,600 --> 00:03:22,740
What is it, Chief?

55
00:03:22,740 --> 00:03:24,680
Don't go calling it "athletic" or whatever.

56
00:03:24,680 --> 00:03:26,820
I've never actually eaten one, though.

57
00:03:26,820 --> 00:03:30,800
Before you train your body,
you should train your head.

58
00:03:30,800 --> 00:03:33,920
It's not a food, senpai.

59
00:03:33,920 --> 00:03:35,940
An athletic club is

60
00:03:35,940 --> 00:03:39,540
a place where you do sports
for fitness and health.

61
00:03:40,220 --> 00:03:42,140
with the latest fitness machines

62
00:03:42,140 --> 00:03:44,440
and computerized fitness assessments,

63
00:03:44,440 --> 00:03:47,520
so you can build your
fitness scientifically.

64
00:03:48,960 --> 00:03:50,520
You know they charge money for it, right?

65
00:03:51,380 --> 00:03:54,940
How ridiculous.
Paying money just to exercise.

66
00:03:55,360 --> 00:03:57,180
You just don't get it, Ryo-chan.

67
00:03:57,460 --> 00:04:00,740
Spending money on beauty
and health is common sense.

68
00:04:01,340 --> 00:04:05,200
In Europe and America, people who can't quit smoking
and people who are obese

69
00:04:05,620 --> 00:04:07,935
are seen as people who can't
even manage their own bodies,

70
00:04:07,985 --> 00:04:10,600
and they can't become elite businessmen.

71
00:04:10,680 --> 00:04:11,180
Exactly.

72
00:04:12,520 --> 00:04:15,335
Ryotsu, who has no self-discipline at all,

73
00:04:15,385 --> 00:04:17,160
should definitely try it once.

74
00:04:17,160 --> 00:04:20,640
I don't need to go to a place like that.
I have plenty of stamina.

75
00:04:21,080 --> 00:04:26,020
You idiot! I'm saying you need exercise
that's scientifically calculated.

76
00:04:26,020 --> 00:04:30,820
With all due respect, in my view,
that's like throwing money down the drain.

77
00:04:31,260 --> 00:04:36,480
What did you say? Fine, then let's settle
who has more stamina with an athletic course.

78
00:04:36,480 --> 00:04:39,660
Stop this competition.
It's childish for an adult.

79
00:04:39,660 --> 00:04:42,180
So you're chickening out?

80
00:04:42,180 --> 00:04:43,640
Say it as many times as you like.

81
00:04:44,300 --> 00:04:47,700
What's the fun in wasting
so much energy like that?

82
00:04:47,700 --> 00:04:48,580
How ridiculous.

83
00:04:49,880 --> 00:04:53,120
After all, you're always all talk, you know.

84
00:04:53,700 --> 00:04:56,700
Well, the result is obvious,
so there's no need to even compete.

85
00:04:56,700 --> 00:04:59,880
Fine, I accept your challenge.

86
00:05:00,280 --> 00:05:01,600
So you're fired up now

87
00:05:01,600 --> 00:05:03,160
Don't come crying to me when you regret it.

88
00:05:03,160 --> 00:05:05,820
After all, my stamina is right here,

89
00:05:06,280 --> 00:05:09,160
as proven, it's on par with a 35-year-old's.

90
00:05:09,160 --> 00:05:11,940
But please let me choose the venue.

91
00:05:13,640 --> 00:05:15,760
At Athletic Square,
starting tomorrow at 2 o'clock.

92
00:05:15,760 --> 00:05:17,000
Fine by me.

93
00:05:19,360 --> 00:05:20,800
You'd better be ready, Ryotsu.

94
00:05:23,880 --> 00:05:26,020
What's gotten into you
all of a sudden, senpai?

95
00:05:26,020 --> 00:05:27,740
Something's fishy here.

96
00:05:27,740 --> 00:05:30,460
No, no, no, it's nothing, nothing at all!

97
00:05:30,460 --> 00:05:32,120
What's this?

98
00:05:35,920 --> 00:05:38,640
Kameari Athletic Square
Grand Opening Commemoration

99
00:05:38,640 --> 00:05:40,580
¥1 Million Prize Scramble Event

100
00:05:41,180 --> 00:05:42,760
So this is what you were after.

101
00:05:43,640 --> 00:05:45,260
I knew something was off.

102
00:05:45,260 --> 00:05:46,720
I'm getting mad, Chief.

103
00:05:46,720 --> 00:05:50,260
What? It just so happens there's a prize on the athletic course,
that's all.

104
00:06:02,880 --> 00:06:05,540
You two don't need to take part too,
you know.

105
00:06:05,540 --> 00:06:08,120
But I want the million yen too!

106
00:06:08,120 --> 00:06:10,080
It'd help pay off the house loan, after all.

107
00:06:10,660 --> 00:06:12,400
Yo! Sorry to keep you waiting.

108
00:06:13,640 --> 00:06:14,440
Everyone's here together

109
00:06:14,440 --> 00:06:18,120
Yes, we thought we'd join in too,
serving as witnesses as well.

110
00:06:18,120 --> 00:06:18,880
I see.

111
00:06:19,700 --> 00:06:21,760
Still, what a big turnout.

112
00:06:21,760 --> 00:06:22,960
Is something going on?

113
00:06:22,960 --> 00:06:24,760
I wonder what it is.

114
00:06:25,220 --> 00:06:27,400
I know that voice...

115
00:06:28,180 --> 00:06:29,780
The Kameari caveman

116
00:06:30,280 --> 00:06:31,780
What, you two came too?

117
00:06:31,780 --> 00:06:35,500
Ugh, running into Ryotsu of all people here.

118
00:06:35,500 --> 00:06:37,980
Seriously, we're here too, you know.

119
00:06:37,980 --> 00:06:39,480
You could just go somewhere else.

120
00:06:39,480 --> 00:06:41,120
Saying whatever you like

121
00:06:41,720 --> 00:06:42,640
Ryo-san.

122
00:06:43,640 --> 00:06:49,400
Well, look who's here. Ramen shop, model shop, liquor store.
Hurry up and pay your tab!

123
00:06:49,400 --> 00:06:52,840
Every time you see us, it's money, money.
Can't you say anything else?

124
00:06:53,240 --> 00:06:57,320
We don't like saying it either.
If you hate it, just pay us back already.

125
00:06:57,320 --> 00:07:01,240
Just wait. Once I get the prize money,
I'll pay you back in full.

126
00:07:01,780 --> 00:07:05,220
Prize money? What are you talking about?
Hey... it's nothing!

127
00:07:09,720 --> 00:07:12,640
Everyone,
thank you so much for coming today.

128
00:07:13,180 --> 00:07:17,160
We will now begin the 1
million yen survival race.

129
00:07:19,860 --> 00:07:20,260
What?

130
00:07:21,240 --> 00:07:23,400
Ryotsu, what is this supposed to mean?

131
00:07:24,900 --> 00:07:27,340
What is this? I had no idea at all.

132
00:07:27,340 --> 00:07:31,460
You used me.
Using healthy sports to make money!

133
00:07:31,460 --> 00:07:34,720
Now, now, Chief.
It's still the same contest, after all.

134
00:07:35,480 --> 00:07:38,400
Or will you admit defeat
without even fighting?

135
00:07:39,540 --> 00:07:41,660
No, I won't lose to you of all people!

136
00:07:41,660 --> 00:07:43,600
Please come up to the entrance now.

137
00:07:44,280 --> 00:07:47,100
Participants,
please change into these inside.

138
00:07:48,940 --> 00:07:49,780
Where is this?

139
00:07:51,820 --> 00:07:52,800
Whoa!

140
00:07:52,800 --> 00:07:53,720
What's this?

141
00:07:55,080 --> 00:07:56,520
It's a cockroach, isn't it!

142
00:07:57,180 --> 00:07:59,000
Then please move over this way.

143
00:07:59,000 --> 00:08:01,620
Why do I have to wear this kind of outfit?

144
00:08:01,620 --> 00:08:02,940
I can't take this anymore.

145
00:08:26,500 --> 00:08:28,200
It's a giant kitchen.

146
00:08:28,200 --> 00:08:29,520
What is this?

147
00:08:29,520 --> 00:08:32,260
So we're going to become cockroaches?

148
00:08:33,940 --> 00:08:36,500
Welcome to the Cockroach Athletic Course,
the best in the 10th!

149
00:08:36,860 --> 00:08:39,880
Through this kitchen diorama,
about twenty times larger,

150
00:08:39,880 --> 00:08:42,720
making your way over countless obstacles,

151
00:08:42,720 --> 00:08:46,160
is truly a simulated
experience of being a cockroach.

152
00:08:47,080 --> 00:08:49,940
Honestly, they went to all this
trouble to build such a thing.

153
00:08:49,940 --> 00:08:52,840
Haha, if you're going to quit,
now's the time.

154
00:08:52,840 --> 00:08:55,700
What? Who said anything about quitting?
Let's have a showdown!

155
00:08:56,360 --> 00:08:59,720
The goal is the anpan in the storage
container on top of the refrigerator.

156
00:09:00,600 --> 00:09:06,700
The first person to reach it
within thirty minutes wins.

157
00:09:07,080 --> 00:09:10,160
There are three courses,
as written on the floor.

158
00:09:10,520 --> 00:09:12,500
You're free to choose
whichever course you like.

159
00:09:12,500 --> 00:09:14,460
Please choose the course you like.

160
00:09:16,700 --> 00:09:19,240
Going straight ahead is the shortest route,
after all.

161
00:09:20,760 --> 00:09:23,420
No, there are far too many openings.

162
00:09:23,420 --> 00:09:25,240
There might be some kind of trap.

163
00:09:27,940 --> 00:09:30,460
Should we go over the sink up above?

164
00:09:33,360 --> 00:09:35,920
Well then, I wish you all the best of luck.

165
00:09:35,920 --> 00:09:37,280
Ready...

166
00:09:40,920 --> 00:09:42,020
Go!

167
00:09:45,420 --> 00:09:46,860
This is the best way.

168
00:09:47,400 --> 00:09:49,060
I'll do my best for Japan!

169
00:09:53,060 --> 00:09:53,620
Look out!

170
00:09:54,580 --> 00:09:55,920
You copied me, Ryotsu!

171
00:09:56,060 --> 00:09:56,780
Let's wake him up!

172
00:10:02,720 --> 00:10:03,240
Leave it to me!

173
00:10:03,720 --> 00:10:04,080
Yeah.

174
00:10:04,540 --> 00:10:09,260
Climbing up is pretty tough, you know.

175
00:10:10,400 --> 00:10:11,720
Straight through the front!

176
00:10:14,540 --> 00:10:15,660
One more to go!

177
00:10:18,920 --> 00:10:22,080
There's an electric cockroach-repellent
device laid across the floor!

178
00:10:22,400 --> 00:10:24,080
How incredibly realistic!

179
00:10:26,520 --> 00:10:28,300
There's no electricity running over here!

180
00:10:35,200 --> 00:10:36,940
It's too dark to see well.

181
00:10:36,940 --> 00:10:39,140
Somehow my tongue feels all sticky.

182
00:10:43,580 --> 00:10:44,460
What is this?

183
00:10:45,340 --> 00:10:47,960
Oh no, could this be...

184
00:10:49,160 --> 00:10:50,940
Isn't this a cockroach love thing?

185
00:10:55,440 --> 00:10:57,020
My tongue is in a panic.

186
00:10:57,020 --> 00:10:58,760
So the sink is the right answer, then.

187
00:11:02,820 --> 00:11:04,420
That 1 million yen is mine!

188
00:11:13,720 --> 00:11:14,440
Help!

189
00:11:15,260 --> 00:11:17,240
Ryo-san, come on, help me out!

190
00:11:17,880 --> 00:11:18,600
Well, let me think.

191
00:11:18,600 --> 00:11:22,560
If you wipe out what I owe you for the model kits and RC cars,
maybe I'll help you.

192
00:11:23,420 --> 00:11:24,520
That's cruel!

193
00:11:24,520 --> 00:11:26,320
Well, then, fine by me.

194
00:11:26,320 --> 00:11:29,240
Wait, wait! Okay, okay, just help me!

195
00:11:29,420 --> 00:11:32,280
Alright then, Gucchan. Here, grab on.

196
00:11:38,840 --> 00:11:39,660
Too late

197
00:11:42,100 --> 00:11:43,760
Sorry, Ryotsu! I'm first!

198
00:11:46,600 --> 00:11:47,780
Damn it.

199
00:11:48,460 --> 00:11:51,760
Looks like it disappears
about once every minute.

200
00:11:52,340 --> 00:11:53,960
We'll push through the
next time it disappears.

201
00:11:53,960 --> 00:11:55,440
It's a full minute!

202
00:11:57,380 --> 00:11:59,500
We can't wait a whole minute!

203
00:12:08,580 --> 00:12:09,920
Unbelievable.

204
00:12:09,920 --> 00:12:11,320
He's not human.

205
00:12:16,520 --> 00:12:18,900
At your age,
you shouldn't push yourself too hard.

206
00:12:26,780 --> 00:12:30,080
Chief, over there's
the wanted criminal Goto!

207
00:12:30,080 --> 00:12:33,500
What? Where? Where?

208
00:12:41,220 --> 00:12:43,520
You can't get through life
on physical strength alone.

209
00:12:43,520 --> 00:12:45,080
You've got to use your brain, too.

210
00:12:46,060 --> 00:12:46,780
Nice.

211
00:12:46,780 --> 00:12:49,880
You're tenacious, aren't you?
Well, I'll go on ahead.

212
00:12:49,880 --> 00:12:51,860
Using such dirty tricks!

213
00:12:57,220 --> 00:12:58,800
Aaaaah!

214
00:12:58,800 --> 00:12:59,760
The culprit at the start...

215
00:12:59,760 --> 00:13:03,280
Chief, no idiot falls
for the same trick twice.

216
00:13:05,500 --> 00:13:07,080
There's ten thousand yen over there.

217
00:13:07,080 --> 00:13:08,040
Ten thousand yen?

218
00:13:10,500 --> 00:13:12,300
What a simple guy.

219
00:13:15,260 --> 00:13:16,400
How about it, Ryotsu!

220
00:13:16,400 --> 00:13:19,060
Try to figure something out with
that brain you're so proud of.

221
00:13:22,100 --> 00:13:23,480
I'm not losing yet!

222
00:13:31,480 --> 00:13:31,860
Over here.

223
00:13:31,860 --> 00:13:35,340
This is nothing!

224
00:13:35,760 --> 00:13:41,460
Ryo-chan's in that cockroach
koi-koi from earlier?

225
00:13:42,694 --> 00:13:46,460
Even Ryotsu couldn't escape from there.

226
00:13:46,460 --> 00:13:49,180
If he's not here, there's no need to panic.

227
00:13:49,580 --> 00:13:52,160
I got a bit carried away
earlier and went too fast.

228
00:14:11,020 --> 00:14:12,020
Aaaaaah!

229
00:14:13,240 --> 00:14:13,480
Aaaaaah!

230
00:14:13,480 --> 00:14:13,980
Aaaaaah!

231
00:14:13,980 --> 00:14:14,220
Aaaaaah!

232
00:14:14,220 --> 00:14:14,280
Aaaaaah!

233
00:14:14,280 --> 00:14:14,340
Aaaaaah!

234
00:14:14,340 --> 00:14:14,460
Aaaaaah!

235
00:14:14,460 --> 00:14:15,520
They're coming at us all at once!

236
00:14:16,560 --> 00:14:18,400
Amazing! He made the impossible possible!

237
00:14:18,760 --> 00:14:21,440
That's truly cockroach-level stamina.

238
00:14:22,360 --> 00:14:24,540
Yeah, that's incredible stamina.

239
00:14:28,280 --> 00:14:30,620
Boss, it's a full-blown high pace,
just as predicted.

240
00:14:30,620 --> 00:14:34,560
At this rate, quite a few people
will reach the goal within 30 minutes.

241
00:14:35,000 --> 00:14:35,360
What?

242
00:14:36,020 --> 00:14:37,720
Didn't I tell you so?

243
00:14:37,740 --> 00:14:40,100
What do you plan to do,
offering a prize like this?

244
00:14:40,800 --> 00:14:44,120
Right now, our household can't
afford to put up any prize money!

245
00:14:44,340 --> 00:14:48,240
Phew, there's no choice.
I never thought I'd have to use this.

246
00:15:02,340 --> 00:15:03,940
I-I'm terribly late.

247
00:15:11,380 --> 00:15:31,060
Aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa!

248
00:15:31,060 --> 00:15:33,140
Look at that!
Feel the power of the robot arm!

249
00:15:34,900 --> 00:15:36,580
Don't be surprised just yet!

250
00:15:38,560 --> 00:15:40,680
The spoons and bridges are in the way.
It's hard to swim!

251
00:15:57,900 --> 00:15:58,820
This is unbearable!

252
00:16:04,140 --> 00:16:06,740
But thanks to that,
the bridge and futon came off.

253
00:16:14,600 --> 00:16:15,360
This way!

254
00:16:16,220 --> 00:16:16,960
Ryo-chan?

255
00:16:17,840 --> 00:16:20,400
What, Nakagawa and the others are here too?

256
00:16:21,420 --> 00:16:24,605
Yes, we were suddenly
attacked and ran in here,

257
00:16:24,655 --> 00:16:25,820
but we can't get out.

258
00:16:28,040 --> 00:16:29,640
Damn it, the one million yen...

259
00:16:29,690 --> 00:16:32,240
We can't be dawdling in a place like this!

260
00:16:32,860 --> 00:16:34,900
Right, everyone, rush out at the same time!

261
00:16:35,740 --> 00:16:38,080
They're machines, they can't move fast.

262
00:16:38,080 --> 00:16:42,060
While someone sacrifices themselves,
the others can move ahead.

263
00:16:42,760 --> 00:16:43,760
Interesting.

264
00:16:44,220 --> 00:16:44,580
Ready?

265
00:16:46,000 --> 00:16:48,540
Listen, if anyone gets taken out,
no hard feelings.

266
00:16:48,540 --> 00:16:48,980
Yeah.

267
00:16:50,540 --> 00:16:51,400
Now! Go!

268
00:16:51,540 --> 00:16:51,900
Right!

269
00:16:52,460 --> 00:16:55,000
Those guys are being attacked. Have at it.

270
00:16:55,420 --> 00:16:56,460
Just as I thought.

271
00:16:58,820 --> 00:17:00,260
Everyone's so unfair!

272
00:17:01,140 --> 00:17:02,920
Who's the one being unfair?

273
00:17:03,220 --> 00:17:04,120
Zaha!

274
00:17:07,920 --> 00:17:08,800
Okay, now!

275
00:17:10,120 --> 00:17:12,640
Damn it! I'm not going down alone!

276
00:17:16,480 --> 00:17:18,545
G-g-

277
00:17:18,595 --> 00:17:21,240
Bakakura!

278
00:17:22,240 --> 00:17:23,220
Aaaaaah!

279
00:17:25,140 --> 00:17:27,180
That's awful, senpai.

280
00:17:27,180 --> 00:17:29,940
Heh, serves you right.
You're no match for me.

281
00:17:37,080 --> 00:17:39,720
How about that? Vertical surfaces are hard to hit,
aren't they?

282
00:17:39,720 --> 00:17:44,940
Chief, you're still alive?
I won't forgive you!

283
00:17:44,940 --> 00:17:45,760
Damn it.

284
00:17:51,160 --> 00:17:53,000
They're sticking to the
wall and moving forward!

285
00:17:53,000 --> 00:17:55,100
They look just like real cockroaches.

286
00:18:09,280 --> 00:18:11,040
They're dropping out one after another.

287
00:18:11,040 --> 00:18:11,640
Go on!

288
00:18:13,540 --> 00:18:14,420
Zatchu Dai Gar!

289
00:18:14,420 --> 00:18:15,040
It's all over.

290
00:18:20,240 --> 00:18:21,640
They won't reach us this far.

291
00:18:25,900 --> 00:18:28,300
Stop following me and
copying everything I do!

292
00:18:28,920 --> 00:18:30,980
You're the one who should
stop pulling dirty tricks!

293
00:18:32,520 --> 00:18:33,340
That's cheating!

294
00:18:37,960 --> 00:18:39,720
So even the senior has
finally been taken down.

295
00:18:39,720 --> 00:18:41,480
And he got so far, too.

296
00:18:43,020 --> 00:18:46,520
Look, he came out from over there!

297
00:18:46,520 --> 00:18:48,180
Moving even better than the real thing!

298
00:18:49,100 --> 00:18:50,940
The Chief's not bad either.

299
00:18:59,440 --> 00:19:00,280
Chief!

300
00:19:00,280 --> 00:19:02,060
It's a present for you!

301
00:19:02,720 --> 00:19:04,180
Please!

302
00:19:11,480 --> 00:19:33,740
Aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaah!

303
00:19:34,740 --> 00:19:36,200
I can't get near those two.

304
00:19:47,080 --> 00:19:50,140
The goal is right in front of me,
and the million yen is mine!

305
00:19:50,140 --> 00:19:51,860
Yo-ots!

306
00:19:53,160 --> 00:19:54,520
No, Chief.

307
00:19:55,220 --> 00:19:56,700
I won't forgive you anymore!

308
00:19:56,700 --> 00:19:59,440
Please calm down, keep your voice down.

309
00:19:59,440 --> 00:20:00,820
What is it?

310
00:20:00,820 --> 00:20:02,060
We've been spotted!

311
00:20:03,060 --> 00:20:04,640
Saved! We've been found!

312
00:20:06,240 --> 00:20:08,640
Damn it! We're so close to the goal!

313
00:20:12,140 --> 00:20:14,200
I'm not letting myself get
beaten after coming this far!

314
00:20:16,220 --> 00:20:17,120
Alright! How about this!

315
00:20:19,560 --> 00:20:22,120
This is disgusting... I'll shake you off!

316
00:20:28,440 --> 00:20:29,580
I'm not falling off!

317
00:20:29,960 --> 00:20:31,680
The Chief got crushed, though.

318
00:20:31,680 --> 00:20:34,100
Who got crushed, you say?

319
00:20:37,080 --> 00:20:38,040
Chief!

320
00:20:38,780 --> 00:20:40,440
I'm not losing yet!

321
00:20:45,220 --> 00:20:46,380
One million yen!

322
00:20:51,200 --> 00:20:52,800
Are you falling?!

323
00:20:53,080 --> 00:20:54,060
One million yen!

324
00:20:56,460 --> 00:20:59,660
How unyielding can you be?
Then how about this?

325
00:21:30,420 --> 00:21:33,420
Aaaaaaah!

326
00:21:39,260 --> 00:21:42,180
This is bad!
At this rate, I'll be attacked someday!

327
00:21:44,440 --> 00:21:45,840
The goal! Chance!

328
00:21:49,720 --> 00:21:51,700
It jumped! How disgusting!

329
00:21:54,640 --> 00:21:56,320
Damn it! Guts!

330
00:22:00,120 --> 00:22:03,660
Yes! One million yen is mine!

331
00:22:12,100 --> 00:22:13,260
For one million yen,

332
00:22:14,740 --> 00:22:17,300
didn't I tell you, Chief?

333
00:22:17,300 --> 00:22:20,840
that paying to play on an athletic
course was a waste of money?

334
00:22:22,080 --> 00:22:24,140
Aren't you going to change clothes, senior?

335
00:22:24,140 --> 00:22:27,200
I liked it, so I took it as a souvenir.

336
00:22:27,800 --> 00:22:30,080
I'll live as a cockroach
for the rest of my life.

337
00:22:30,580 --> 00:22:32,140
Ryo-san, you did it!

338
00:22:32,700 --> 00:22:34,940
Congratulations.

339
00:22:34,940 --> 00:22:36,860
I knew you'd do it.

340
00:22:36,860 --> 00:22:38,420
The promised...

341
00:22:42,920 --> 00:22:45,087
Hey, if you can take it,
then try to grab it!

342
00:22:45,137 --> 00:22:46,940
When it comes to stamina,
I won't lose to anyone.

343
00:22:47,840 --> 00:22:48,520
Whoa, you idiot.

344
00:22:48,900 --> 00:22:52,660
It's one million yen.

345
00:22:54,160 --> 00:22:55,580
This is bad.

346
00:22:56,240 --> 00:22:56,800
Yes!

347
00:23:06,440 --> 00:23:07,240
Hey, you.

348
00:23:13,800 --> 00:23:16,100
What happened to this?

349
00:23:17,040 --> 00:23:18,160
Take a look at this.

350
00:23:19,380 --> 00:23:24,740
Recently, there's been a string of eyewitness reports
of giant cockroaches sighted here on Yumenoshima.

351
00:23:25,340 --> 00:23:31,060
And at last, our news crew succeeded
in capturing one on camera.

352
00:23:31,060 --> 00:23:31,960
Cockroach

353
00:23:31,960 --> 00:23:34,880
Now, please take a look
at this shocking footage.

354
00:23:39,380 --> 00:23:40,620
Aaaaaah!

355
00:23:40,620 --> 00:23:42,420
1 million yen!

356
00:23:42,420 --> 00:23:45,700
My 1 million yen!

357
00:23:47,280 --> 00:23:50,400
Damn it, where did it go?

358
00:23:50,400 --> 00:23:52,280
My 1 million yen!

359
00:24:03,980 --> 00:24:06,560
Aaah, what do I do?

360
00:24:07,240 --> 00:24:10,700
I messed up developing the important
photos the Chief asked me for!

361
00:24:11,040 --> 00:24:13,040
Bad! Bad! Bad!

362
00:24:13,240 --> 00:24:14,560
If this gets out, I'm not getting off easy!

363
00:24:14,780 --> 00:24:16,980
I've got to cover this up no matter what!

364
00:24:17,300 --> 00:24:20,820
Next time: a recreation of the Kyoto trip!
See you then!

365
00:24:29,720 --> 00:24:32,700
Even if I try to stop the clocks,

366
00:24:34,340 --> 00:24:37,760
time keeps on passing.

367
00:24:39,360 --> 00:24:42,600
Scrunching up my face and crying,

368
00:24:44,420 --> 00:24:48,000
let's laugh it off and keep on living.

369
00:24:50,380 --> 00:24:53,020
Even if today

370
00:24:55,440 --> 00:24:57,920
is a rainy day,

371
00:24:57,920 --> 00:25:03,440
tomorrow will be sunny.

372
00:25:03,440 --> 00:25:08,620
Bye-bye, let's wave our hands.

373
00:25:08,620 --> 00:25:13,860
Unpleasant things, goodbye.

374
00:25:14,420 --> 00:25:18,720
Oh yeah, live as you like.

375
00:25:18,720 --> 00:25:23,940
Let's try living, good things will come.

376
00:25:23,940 --> 00:25:30,260
Outside the door, the sun is calling you.

